# DEMO 3: Write code and verify it yourself
#
# builder writes the code, compiles it, reads gcc's errors, fixes them,
# recompiles - until it works. Then it RUNS it to verify the output.
# tester writes separate tests and runs them.
#
# What you see: the agent does not write code "blind". It sees the real
# compiler errors and fixes them. That is the difference between a text
# generator and a programmer.
#
# Run:
#   ./pixelgo flow run demo demo/03-build-verify.flow "Write a program that prints the first 20 Fibonacci numbers"

entry builder

node builder
node tester

edge builder -> tester
edge tester  -> END
